# several steps held: an edit is on them all. A later step held with the first alone and let go with nothing
# edited is the first's length (as before); turn a knob meanwhile and it was a pair instead, and no release
# toggles a step. An earlier step, or a third, is always held with the others
wait 300
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 2
notes 2 1 1 1 100 60
notes 2 1 5 1 100 62
notes 2 1 9 1 100 64
# the length gesture, unchanged: hold step 1, tap step 4
key w0 down
wait 60
tapkey w3
key w0 up
expect slen 2 1 16
expect note 2 1 4 0
expect note 2 1 1 60
# a pair: hold 1 and 5, turn LENGTH: both change; neither is toggled, and 5 is no length
key w0 down
wait 30
key w4 down
wait 30
spin K2 2
wait 30
key w4 up
key w0 up
expect slen 2 1 18
expect slen 2 5 6
expect note 2 1 1 60
expect note 2 1 5 62
# an earlier step joins (5 held, then 1): no length, the knob moves both
key w4 down
wait 30
key w0 down
wait 30
spin K2 1
key w0 up
key w4 up
expect slen 2 1 19
expect slen 2 5 7
expect note 2 1 1 60
# three: 1, 5, 9 held; let go with nothing edited: no length, no toggle
key w0 down
wait 30
key w4 down
wait 30
key w8 down
wait 30
key w8 up
key w4 up
key w0 up
expect slen 2 1 19
expect note 2 1 1 60
expect note 2 1 5 62
expect note 2 1 9 64
# three, with the pitch knob: all three up a semitone
key w0 down
key w4 down
key w8 down
wait 30
spin K4 1
key w0 up
key w4 up
key w8 up
expect note 2 1 1 61
expect note 2 1 5 63
expect note 2 1 9 65
# the first let go before the later one, nothing edited: still the length
key w0 down
wait 30
key w2 down
wait 30
key w0 up
key w2 up
expect slen 2 1 12
expect note 2 1 3 0
# a kit: a black key with two steps held puts the sound on both
turn ALGO -1
expect trk 1
key w0 down
key w6 down
wait 30
tapkey b2
key w6 up
key w0 up
expect note 1 1 1 3
expect note 1 1 7 3
